<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49961" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ūsūrārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		usura. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>That serves</i> or <i>is fit for
			use</i>, <i>of which one has the use</i> or <i>enjoyment</i>, = usuarius: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puer,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Curc. 3, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uxor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Am. 1, 2, 36</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to
			interest</i> or <i>usury</i>, <i>that
				pays interest</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Truc. 1, 1, 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pecunia,</span>”
				<i>at interest</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					16, 2, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">debitum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 3,
					5, 5 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">3, 5, 37</span></i>
			<i>fin.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">debitor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib.
					21, 1, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
